.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt IMP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imp
.Nd media dispatcher for the Redhot suite
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar file
.Nm
.Cm \-\-dry-run
.Ar file
.Nm
.Cm \-\-list-mappings
.Nm
.Cm \-\-list-handlers
.Nm
.Cm \-\-selftest
.Nm
.Cm \-\-version
.Nm
.Cm \-\-help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
receives a file path, decides which application should open it,
and delegates execution without an intermediate shell.
.Pp
.Nm
never modifies the file.
It opens, delegates, and exits.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm \-\-dry-run
Print the dispatch plan to stdout without executing the handler.
.It Cm \-\-config Ar path
Use an alternate
.Pa imp.conf .
.It Cm \-\-debug
Enable debug\-level logging to stderr for this invocation.
.It Cm \-\-json
Emit JSON instead of plain text (valid with
.Cm \-\-list-mappings ,
.Cm \-\-list-handlers ,
and
.Cm \-\-selftest ) .
.It Cm \-\-list-mappings
Print every loaded rule as
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar command .
.It Cm \-\-list-handlers
Print every handler with its availability (OK/MISSING).
.It Cm \-\-selftest
Report on the runtime environment. Exit 0 if required items are present.
.It Cm \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.It Cm \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/redhot/imp/imp.conf
Per\-user configuration.
.It Pa /etc/redhot/imp/imp.conf
System configuration (Debian, OpenBSD).
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/redhot/imp/imp.conf
System configuration (FreeBSD).
.It Pa ~/.config/redhot/imp/mime.types
Auxiliary extension\-to\-MIME map.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Handler executed successfully, or dry\-run completed.
.It 1
No rule matched and no fallback is configured.
.It 2
All handlers in the chain failed to execute.
.It 3
File missing, unreadable, or is a directory.
.It 4
Configuration invalid.
.It 5
Interrupted (SIGINT).
.It 64
Usage error.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr file 1 ,
.Xr xdg-open 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The RedhotBSD Authors
